-- Forever quests, quest NPCs, objects, drops and vendors that fresh installs have been missing since 0.1.28.
-- Player report 2026-11-05 (bug-report forum, "Quest Progression Issues Across Multiple Races and Zones"): quest chains stop
-- early in the starting zones, Westfall, Redridge, Dun Morogh, Loch Modan and more, and players run out of quests around level 14.
-- Cause: 21 world files with Forever quest data (first shipped 2026-10-26, ported from AnoCore, credit to the AnoCore project)
-- were taken out of sql/custom on 2026-10-30, and the owner decision of 2026-10-31 to keep that data in never put them back.
-- Installs that started on 0.1.27 or older still have the data; installs that started on 0.1.28 or newer never got it, and
-- the shipped database dump is older than those files. On a fresh 0.1.30 world this restores about 100 quests a player
-- can pick up and finish (for example Elwynn 91724 Delicate Instruments, Westfall 92745-92753 Moonbrook/Deadmines chain,
-- Dun Morogh 98326 Frosthowl, Loch Modan 86758 Twisting the Knife, Redridge 98387 Blackrock Blockade, Wetlands 98072).
-- How it was made: a fresh 0.1.30 world (base + every sql/custom/world file) was compared with the same build that also
-- had the 21 files applied in their place in the update order. Only rows that differ are written here, so every fix we
-- made after 2026-10-26 stays as it is. Each changed key is deleted and written again, so it is safe to run more than
-- once and gives the same result on a fresh install, on an update from 0.1.28-0.1.30 and on an older install.
-- Checked: run twice on a scratch copy of the 0.1.30 world; afterwards all 46 tables match the reference row for row.


